WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:08.599
Joseph in Joseph says, Hey David, why will
stupid Democrats like Bernie and Warren insist

00:00:08.599 --> 00:00:14.610
on weakening our military? This is one of
those questions that really requires a little

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.840
bit of historical context to understand. And
the historical context is that going back

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:28.210
decades now, there has been an attempt from
the right to feminize the left. And, uh, what

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:33.809
we're really talking about is the feminization
of democratic male candidates. If you look

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:41.769
at 2004, uh, and you look at John Kerry, John
Kerry was a military veteran. The right loves

00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:46.749
to talk about so-called war heroes. We can
debate whether somebody who served in the

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:50.539
military is or isn't a war hero by default.

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:55.670
Reasonable people can argue about that is
merely serving your country. An act of heroism

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.350
does it depending on what you, whatever, right?
The conversation doesn't matter by the definition

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:07.451
that the right used. John Kerry was a war
hero. Uh, and yet they feminized him. They

00:01:07.451 --> 00:01:13.650
talked about him speaking French. They talked
about him, you know, being European in whatever

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:21.380
ways they minimized his, uh, military credentials.
The Swift boat veterans, uh, came out and

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:26.980
attacked, carry around his claims regarding
military service. And this is all part of

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:34.540
this, uh, movement that exists to feminize
the left as being afraid of war, as being

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:40.650
afraid of guns, as shying away irrationally
from violence. So that's where you get questions

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:48.300
like this. Why will Democrats weaken our military?
And of course, the truth is that our military

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:54.830
is so over-funded. It is so many orders of
magnitude inflated beyond what it needs to

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:58.720
be to still be the strongest and biggest military
in the world.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.670
That anyone who says, you know what, I'm concerned
about how much we're spending on the military.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:08.250
I'm concerned about the foreign policy, the
moral, the legal, the ethical implications

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:15.639
of how far the tentacles of our military spread.
They are accused like what we are seeing here

00:02:15.639 --> 00:02:22.379
of wanting to weaken our military when the
truth is that, uh, even significant cuts to

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:26.489
the military would not weaken the military.
The U S would be more than able to protect

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:29.599
itself from any kind of attack. But there's
another element that I want to talk about

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:35.639
here. Uh, there's this idea that a democratic
president like Bernie or Warren, the right

00:02:35.639 --> 00:02:43.099
likes to push this. If push came to shove
and the correct decision was a military engagement,

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:48.879
they simply wouldn't do it. They paint a picture
of potential democratic presidents as people

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:56.239
who the U S would be under attack domestically.
One of our allies of base whatever.

00:02:56.239 --> 00:03:01.169
And the military would come to president Bernie
Sanders or Elizabeth Warren. They say, Madam

00:03:01.169 --> 00:03:05.419
president, mr president, we're under attack.
We've got to do something. And Bernier Warren

00:03:05.419 --> 00:03:10.670
would sit back and say, no, we're not going
to do anything. We will allow ourselves to

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:16.269
simply be attacked and people to be killed.
This is not how things work. I know that with

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:22.200
Donald Trump who operates unilaterally going
completely against the recommendations of

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.659
the Pentagon and the state department and
whoever it seems as though that's something

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:31.180
that presidents typically do. The reality
is that both Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:38.049
Warren have made no indication that they are
a pacifists, a priori, and they have made

00:03:38.049 --> 00:03:43.799
it abundantly clear that if they were president,
when military advisers come to them and they

00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:50.010
explain the situation on the ground, they
would basically follow the advice of their

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:54.620
generals as Donald Trump likes to say. So
the question is problematic.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:04:01.400
At its core, it relates to this historical
feminization and weakening that Republicans

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:07.069
have sort of successfully done the Democrats
when it comes to foreign policy because Hey,

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:13.109
Democrats don't want illegal Wars, never ending
Wars occupations in the wrong country that

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:19.780
didn't actually do all of that stuff they've
feminized. And may framed as weak Democrats.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:25.170
But more importantly, they also liked to pretend
that a progressive president, like a Bernie

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:30.690
or a Warren would ignore the advice of experts.
If anything, the problem we have right now

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:35.730
is that Trump ignores advice from experts.
Bernie or Warren would actually listen to

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.080
what experts are saying, and we should be
glad for that. So Joseph, I don't know if

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:42.890
you're asking this question in good faith
or not, uh, but assuming that it's in good

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:47.120
faith, you appear to have been bamboozled
by some of the right wing talking points on

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.970
this issue that does it

